## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of fast, branchless bit tricks and constant-time bit-scanning utilities common in high-performance systems.

## Key Concepts
- Isolating least-significant 1: v = n & -n
- De Bruijn-based indexing: map a 5-bit index to a trailing-zero count
- Handling edge case n == 0 (return 32)
- Static lookup table of 32 entries

## Code Example
```c
uint32_t countTrailingZeros32(uint32_t n){
  static const int debruijn[32] = {0,1,28,2,29,14,24,3,30,22,20,15,25,17,4,8,31,27,13,23,21,19,16,7,26,12,18,9,6,11,5,10};
  if(n == 0) return 32;
  uint32_t v = n & -n;
  return debruijn[(v * 0x077CB531) >> 27];
}
```

